  "description": "A gap in the stream positions of a drive: D wire frames start the drive and insert positions with the frame's elevation (30, 32); then the stream sends no D/N/R frame while D polls keep coming. Every poll coordinate has a declared terrain elevation. The first two polls after the last stream position stay without elevation, from the third on a poll gets the terrain elevation (61, 58). A further D frame (elevation 40) starts the count over: the next poll and the closing P poll stay without elevation. The drive's ascent (31) and descent (21) include the gap. The car position stored on returning to online stays without elevation. Ends asleep so the replay stays repeat-neutral; the asleep terminal is reached from :online and is therefore awaited.",
